## Layout (docx_builder skeleton)

This project uses a role-based layout: each directory is a role in a pipeline.
**Take only the layers you need; absent layers simply do not exist.** The list
below describes every possible layer, so this file stays valid for any subset
and never needs regenerating when a layer is added later. Check which directories
are actually present before assuming one exists.

- `report/` the build: `content.yaml` produces the document into `output/`
  (`.docx`, plus `.pdf` on macOS).
  - `report/images/` rendered figures referenced by `content.yaml`.
  - `report/assets/` editable figure sources (html, svg, xlsx, diagrams).
  - `report/output/` generated `.docx` and `.pdf`.
  - `report/templates/` cover `.docx` templates, if any.
  - `report/ai-check/` output of any AI-detection tooling (present with the `ai-check` layer).
- `references/` reference and source material you consulted.
- `brief/` the brief or instructions you are working from.
- `src/` your work product: code, data, whatever you produce.
- `tools/` automation scripts (see "Prereqs" below):
  - `tools/monitor/` screenshot intake.
  - `tools/ai-detection/` AI-detection drivers; their output goes to `report/ai-check/`.
- `meta/` checklist, notes, metadata.
- `.work/` transient scratch space (gitignored).

## Build

```bash
docx_builder build .          # build the .docx (finalizes the TOC via Word on macOS)
docx_builder build . --pdf    # build and export to PDF (macOS + Word)
docx_builder validate .       # fail on em/en dash and other AI-tells in prose
```

`build` resolves `content.yaml` from this directory, falling back to `report/`.
Drop figures into `report/images/` and keep their editable sources in `report/assets/`.

## Prereqs for tools/ (only if you use them)

`uv` and `claude-code` are required to run anything under `tools/`. AI-detection
additionally needs a Chrome or Chromium with remote debugging plus network access.
These are optional and only needed when you actually run those tools.

